§ OBLIGATION-MODE SEMANTICS FIX (T26.1 discovery)
  Before Session-8 : all obligations asserted `¬φ` expecting Unsat=success
  After  Session-8 : two-mode system
    Consistency  assert φ ; Sat=success (refinement-self-consistent)
                            Unsat=failure (self-contradiction)
    Verification assert ¬φ ; Unsat=success (φ holds)
                             Sat=failure (counter-example)
  morpheme-bindings → Consistency (they ARE refinements, not proof-obligations)
  div-nonzero / array-bounds → Verification (classical Hoare-style)
  Discharge_Result.ok_count/failure_count/inconclusive_count classification
  exit-code : failure_count > 0 OR (strict && inconclusive_count > 0)

